## 6. Safety Warnings

### 6.1 General Safety
- Always follow proper archery safety procedures
- Wear appropriate safety equipment
- Never dry-fire a bow (shoot without an arrow)
- Keep arrows away from the bowstring when adjusting equipment
- Ensure your shooting area is safe and clear

### 6.2 Equipment Modifications
- Making incorrect adjustments can damage your bow
- Improper tuning can cause injury
- When in doubt, consult a certified bow technician
- Some adjustments (especially cam timing) should only be done by professionals

### 6.3 Professional Help
We strongly recommend consulting a certified bow technician or pro shop for:
- Cam timing adjustments
- Major equipment changes
- If you're unsure about any adjustment
- Complex tuning issues

